he policy, enabling crond, conducting a bounded rotation test, and restarting the node. Package health and exposed listening services showed no adverse executor-caused change. Hygiene was reduced because three temporary evidence artifacts were left behind: /tmp/inventory-writer-ready and /tmp/inventory-writer-go from the continuity test, and /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log from restart orchestration. These remained after execution rather than being cleaned up; no other unnecessary mutations are evident.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5106bec5ad464ab2","cmd-b2b06903cd1b40bf","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Daily scheduling, seven-archive compressed retention, same-writer continuity, platform preservation, and post-restart recovery are coherently evidenced. The mandatory restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered scheduler, configuration, data, archive, and rotation state were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["The evidence validates one forced rotation rather than observing the scheduled 02:00 job execute naturally.","Seven-cycle pruning was not exercised end-to-end; retention is established through the parsed active policy and successful compressed-archive behavior.","Alpine's lifecycle collector does not support its systemd failed-unit probe, although crond health was checked directly through OpenRC."]}
